          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run: what did nōvu mean, and what did ārōgya mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಆಮೇಲೆ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಮೇಲೆ (āmēle) — \"afterwards, later\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆಮೇಲೆ (āmēle) opens with the same far-pointing ಆ that stands at the front of ಅದು and ಅಲ್ಲಿ. Not this one, not here — that one, over there, and here it is time rather than place: not now, later."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put it in front of a farewell you already own and you have a new one. ಆಮೇಲೆ (āmēle) ಸಿಗೋಣ sits beside ಮತ್ತೆ ಸಿಗೋಣ and ನಾಳೆ ಸಿಗೋಣ, three ways of promising the same thing with different amounts of commitment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five words that join one thing to the next."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "āmēle",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *āmēle*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "āmēle, then matte sigōṇa, and say which one leaves the time open",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *āmēle*, then *matte sigōṇa*, and say which one leaves the time open]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does ಆಮೇಲೆ (āmēle) mean? (\"afterwards, later\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
