          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಇನ್ನೂ (innū) — \"still, yet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಇನ್ನೂ (innū) is the word for a thing that has not stopped or has not started. With ಇಲ್ಲ behind it you get not yet, which is the single most useful thing in this chapter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It stacks with the measuring words from the replies chapter. ಇನ್ನೂ (innū) ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ is a little more still; ಇನ್ನೂ (innū) ಹೆಚ್ಚು is more than that again. One word in front and your five replies have doubled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
