          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಬೇಗ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬೇಗ (bēga) — \"soon, quickly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬೇಗ (bēga) is inherited, and it holds hurry and nearness-in-time on one shape. ಬೇಗ (bēga) ಬಾ is come quickly and equally come soon, and which one is meant is settled by everything around it rather than by the word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set it against īga, the now-word from the leave-taking chapter. Īga is this moment. ಬೇಗ (bēga) is a moment that has not arrived but will not keep you waiting. They rhyme and are unrelated, which by now should surprise you less than it did."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
